class SourceReadServiceStub:
    """---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Read plane — external consumers subscribe to a source's sample stream.

    The mirror of ingest: ingest (SourceIngestService) is client->server (the
    server is a sink); read is server->client (the server is a source). The
    bus-side primitive already exists in-process as SourceSession.subscribe with
    per-subscriber fan-out; this service is its network front for external clients
    (e.g. a customer robot receiving actions an in-Loop control loop produces, or
    a client pulling inference outputs published as a source).

    Open ownership: this is an ATTACH-ONLY read path. A reader never opens a
    source. Opening (starting a source's stream) is owned by the producing/session
    side, in both consume flows:
    1. External RCI reading policy actions: the action source is a paired output
    of the reader's OWN producer (observation) session — opened by that
    session's lifecycle, not here.
    2. Internal RCI, external robot reading actions: the operator/rollout
    lifecycle owns open; the robot only attaches.
    An unopened source is reported as SubscribeEvent.state = STREAM_STATE_FAILED;
    it is never opened on demand by Subscribe.
    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

    """

    def __init__(self, channel):
        """Constructor.

        Args:
            channel: A grpc.Channel.
        """
        self.Subscribe = channel.unary_stream('/loop.edge.source.v1.SourceReadService/Subscribe', request_serializer=v1_dot_source__ingest__pb2.SubscribeRequest.SerializeToString, response_deserializer=v1_dot_source__ingest__pb2.SubscribeEvent.FromString, _registered_method=True)

